> classes are skills (weapon choice and spells) and quest (nemesis and 
> artifact). Tourists have it good for all of these - good weapon choice, 
> good spells, easy nemesis, great Quest Artifact. What more could you want?

Early game equipment.  Valks and Sams start out well armed.  You can, with a
Valk, just go hack-n-slash and usually get quite far before the difficulty
curve catches up with you.  Tourists start the game wanting for more offensive
and defensive capability, and must play the early game very carefully.  Valk
is the easiest class to first ascend, because hack-n-slash tactics are
straight forward, while the more ranged tactics that you need to use to keep
an early Wiz or Tourist alive are more varied.  After a few dozen ascensions,
a player's style has usually blended and sharpened enough that they adapt to
the role they're playing without even realizing.

